    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Quail Creek Golf & Country Club opened in late 1961 after land from Browne farm was sold for a country club and homes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.quailcreek.org/history",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The club’s first greens superintendent was Ken Hubble, and head pro Ernie Vossler, later married to LPGA champion Marlene Hagge, led early years.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        14,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quail_Creek_Golf_%26_Country_Club",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Groundbreaking for the club occurred Nov 30, 1960, with a 40,000‑sq‑ft building designed by Howard, Samis and Davies at an estimated $860,000 cost.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quail_Creek_Golf_%26_Country_Club",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Quail Creek neighborhood, now a hub of northwest Oklahoma City, began as a rural area surrounded by farmland before phased development added streets and utilities.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.quailcreek.org/history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The club hosted the Oklahoma City Open from 1962 to 1967, where Arnold Palmer won in 1964 and Tony Lema in 1966.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quail_Creek_Golf_%26_Country_Club",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "In 1999, a total course renovation finished, updating the historic 1960s layout for modern play.",
